# Benchmark results (generated artifacts)
packages/bench/results/
packages/benchmark/benchmark-results/
# Where `e2e/startupBenchmark.mjs` and `e2e/completionBenchmark.mjs` write every
# run they make. Untracked because a measurement of one machine on one afternoon
# is not a repository artifact, and because `git add -A` after a benchmark run
# otherwise sweeps one in — which is exactly what happened, and had to be
# reverted. The pinned baselines beside it are committed deliberately.
packages/vue-vscode/e2e/benchmarks/results/

# Dependency trees the E2E fixture harness moved out of a fixture. Kept until
# somebody asks for them to go (`test:e2e:fixtures:clean-quarantine`), and inside
# the repository so the rename that fills them cannot cross a device — which is
# precisely why they have to be ignored rather than merely untracked.
/.verter-e2e-quarantine/
# A rollback's undo buffer, alive for one install and removed with it. Only a
# killed run leaves one, and the next run for that fixture recovers it.
node_modules.verter-rollback-*

# Integration test cloned repos
.integration-tests/

# Local analysis-campaign inputs (corpus paths live here, never committed).
# Ignore the directory CONTENTS (not the dir itself) so the lone committable
# example can be re-included — a `!` negation cannot re-include a file whose
# PARENT directory is excluded, so this must be `.analysis/*`, never `.analysis/`.
.analysis/*
!.analysis/projects.local.json.example

